title: NetBird: API Connectivity
agents: netbird
catalog: cloud/netbird
license: GPLv3
distribution: cmk-netbird (community)

item:
 None. There is one service per NetBird account (Checkmk host).

description:
 This check shows whether the special agent could read the NetBird REST API.

 The service is {OK} if all requests succeeded. It is {CRIT} if the API could not
 be queried at all: connection error, timeout, HTTP 401/403 (token invalid,
 expired, or the role is not allowed to read this data), rate limiting after one
 retry, server errors (5xx) or invalid JSON. The error text is shown in the
 summary.

 If only some requests failed (for example the tokens of one user could not be
 read) the service is {WARN} and lists the failed parts, while all remaining data
 is still processed.

 The API does not tell which token a request used. The agent therefore
 assumes that the token it authenticates with is the most recently used, unexpired
 token of the authenticating user. If that token expires within the configured
 levels (default {WARN} at 30 days, {CRIT} at 7 days) the service changes state.
 If the choice is not unambiguous the text says "probable".

 The API token is never part of any output.

discovery:
 One service is created per host that has the NetBird special agent configured.
